If everybody thinks you are crazy, doing something unusual, that's a good signal, keep doing' it.
Fifth point.
First inside, then outside.
If you want to change what's inside of you, you have to work on yourself.
interior work is needed.
We can't change from the outside, we start inside then we go out.
Last point, we have to stop telling ourselves lies
That's the key point, I left it on the last section because we always lie ourselves: “We can’t do that, it’s too difficult” and so on.
That’s not true.
We can do something every time we want it.
The usual excuse, "I have no time" is just not true.
The only truth is, there's no more time to tell ourselves lies, nor for excuses.
