"Yay," he says so delighted, then he asks, "What else?" "I'm reading 8,000 books, and I'm talking to other 150 people." Human beings are way better than machines at computing but worse at memorizing.
I can't even remember my mobile phone. I know my wife's, but I can hardly remember my daughter's.
There's no comparison between human beings' memory and the machines one.
The computing power is growing exponentially: who defeated the World's Chess Champion some years ago was called Deep Blue, he weighed 1.4 tons.
Today, that phone you have in your pocket, 1/10 of your phone is more powerful that that machine.
All of the computing power which took man to the Moon in '69, today is contained in a tiny fraction of the computing power of your smartphone, more or less smart.
