But if biologically we can say little, science can instead prove, just as boldly, what the first word uttered by a human being was: "Change".
Ever since they came to Earth, men and women always had
something to complain. They looked around and took on complaining: the sun could have been a little rounder; the sea could have been less salty; summer could last a little longer, the week could have at least three Sundays.
And so on and so forth.
Nothing was ever fine for them.
One could say, men are born unhappy and with a craving for change.
Change, change, change, change.
And beside being unhappy, men and women have always been picky, too.
Mind you, even the garden of Heaven wasn't good enough for them.
One might say: "Ah, lucky you!
You live in paradise!"
"Yes, it's true," he said, "but we're not the owners." (Laughter) "We're just renting."
(Laughter) "Yes, you're renting, but in paradise, not the outskirts of Milan."
"Yes, but you can't understand.
The owner is such a pain in the neck: you can't touch that stuff, you can't eat that fruit.
Sorry, you rent me a garden and rather than allowing me to eat you'd rather have those four rennet apples rotting?
