Heck, didn't you know?
The iPhone has to be changed!
The diet, the members of the Board,
the coach on the bench,
the striker, the striker's wife.
(Laughter) Nose, boobs, ass, cheekbones!
(Applause) Change the wife, or the husband as the case may be.
Ah, how sexy change is.
And it is since my hearing developed that I hear phrases like: "Either you change, or you’ll be sent to a boarding school!"
It was my mum, unhappy with my marks at school.
"If you don't change your attitude to me, you'll no longer set foot in this house!"
It was my mother who was mad with my dad's mum.
My granny, the mother-in-law.
"If you don't switch channels, you'll not see this face anymore!"
It was mum who was mad with dad because he always watched Domenica Sportiva.
Me, dad and granny have always been very sensitive to change.
(Laughter) And at the same time we have always perceived change as something threatening.
Ever since Amintore Fanfani was Prime Minister, 1959, I was three years old, I have heard on television every week politicians' calls for change, the need and the joint commitment of all parliamentary forces to implement major reforms.
Everyone calls for change, everyone feels the need for the new.
The planet calls for a turnaround, eating habits must be changed, lifestyle has to be changed, the request rises, the nuisance becomes unbearable.
The slogan is clear: from fashion to ecology, politics and morality, from customs to philosophy, from economics to education, change is needed!
But why?
Why is the world so unhappy?
Why are people unsatisfied with their life?
Because man is always disappointed by his possessions?
Are we romantic existentialists who can't bear the obsolescence of things?
Death grieves us, and so we try to remove a natural event with a replacement?
Bah.
Anyhow, if there's one thing that doesn't suffer from existentialism and romanticism, that's the economy, Which is rightfully the true science of change.
They realised, if a car was forever, or a washing machine lasted a century, where would the dividends be found to give to shareholders?
So, buy another washing machine!
Actually, change the way of doing laundry.
(Laughter) Renew your spin-dryer, reform your laundry space.
Revolutionise the washing of coloureds.
Scrap that fucking washing machine!
(Laughter) (Applause) Scrap, to
Mind you, getting money to make you change.
All the way up to the masterpiece of change: planned obsolescence.
If you don't want to change the washing machine, we'll make you change it.
(Laughter) Neither does finance suffer from romance.
Even the way of conceiving savings has led us to change.
Once, once upon a time, if you saved you were virtuous.
They taught you that from childhood, in primary school.
They gave you the piggy bank.
Now, if you keep money, it's trouble.
Spend your money, make the economy run, help to raise the consumption index, otherwise you're an enemy of the nation.
I can imagine it, one day on the news, the anchorman is all sad, comes out and announces, "The President of the Republic has called a day tomorrow of national mourning.
Retail consumption has fallen by 0.3%".
They call us every day to remind us that we must change.
