The voice is an emotional instrument.
All voices are emotional instruments. When we think about the voice, we are used to thinking that it is something external.
There are singers who sing.
Their voice is an emotional instrument
but also your voice is.
We all have a voice, and we communicate through it.
It's a bit like a second skin. It is a point of contact between us and other people.
But unlike the skin, our voice tells us a lot of things.
It tells much more than what we would like to tell.
We lost many memories but the voice did not.
Our voice can remember so many things about our childhood and growth;
We hear a lot of voices during the day.
