The voice of a speaking person contains, somehow, their own story.
It gives information on that person.
We consider it as an organic ringtone of who is in front of us but it is something a little deeper.
We hear broken, hoarse voices voices in transit between one age and another, voices which change with aging.
We hear lots of voices.
I'm fascinated by this thing.
The voice is the window through which I look at the emotionality and the interiority of the human being.
